WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.093
1MDB is one of the biggest frauds,

00:00:04.093 --> 00:00:06.426
financial frauds in history.

00:00:06.426 --> 00:00:09.260
We woke up one morning
in July, 2015, to realize

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.260
that almost $700 million had gone

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:12.718
into the prime minister's account.

00:00:13.218 --> 00:00:15.260
The disappearance of billions of dollars

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.551
from Malaysia's state fund is one

00:00:16.551 --> 00:00:18.885
of the biggest financial scandals,

00:00:18.885 --> 00:00:21.301
not just in Malaysia,
but around the world.

00:00:21.301 --> 00:00:25.343
Of the $8 billion that
1MDB raised via bond sales,

00:00:25.343 --> 00:00:28.093
it's alleged more than half was stolen.

00:00:28.093 --> 00:00:30.010
That's different from a stock fraud

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.176
or pumping up a stock, and then
cashing out on your options.

00:00:33.176 --> 00:00:35.593
This is actual theft of money.

00:00:35.593 --> 00:00:39.385
1MDB in Malaysia had been
actually some kind of

00:00:39.385 --> 00:00:42.260
a piggy bank for various players.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:44.926
The stolen money went
to buy a private jet,

00:00:44.926 --> 00:00:48.760
luxury real estate, artworks
by Picasso and Monet,

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:51.635
as well as jewelry for Mr. Najib's wife.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:55.093
Up to 300,000 taking
to the streets calling

00:00:55.093 --> 00:00:56.676
for Najib's head.

00:00:56.676 --> 00:00:58.551
They are fed up with the government

00:00:58.551 --> 00:01:01.426
that they believe is chronically corrupt.

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.760
The projects that were developed

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:05.968
by 1MDB were sold as

00:01:05.968 --> 00:01:08.343
development projects that
would be to the benefit of everyone,

00:01:08.343 --> 00:01:10.676
but it was later realized that, you know

00:01:10.676 --> 00:01:13.468
it costs the country
probably more than it helped.

00:01:13.468 --> 00:01:15.760
This was cash grab by a handful of people

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.260
who had put themselves in the
position to make themselves rich.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:22.426
It was a betrayal of the
people on a grand scheme.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.468
I arrived at the 1MDB expose

00:01:32.468 --> 00:01:35.010
through a sort of process of having

00:01:35.010 --> 00:01:37.801
started to report on the consequences

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:40.676
of Malaysian corruption on the ground

00:01:40.676 --> 00:01:43.176
that was the destruction
of the Borneo rainforest.

00:01:43.176 --> 00:01:45.968
As I looked into it, it was plainly

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:48.593
caused by political corruption.

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:51.676
There was no logical or sensible reason

00:01:51.676 --> 00:01:53.135
if you were governing the country

00:01:53.135 --> 00:01:56.385
for the benefit of the
democratic electorate

00:01:56.385 --> 00:01:58.260
that you would just rip out a jungle.

00:01:59.176 --> 00:02:01.593
That was done for pure profit

00:02:01.593 --> 00:02:03.801
for a handful of decision-makers.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:05.260
So I started looking at that story

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:06.676
because it was an enormous story

00:02:06.676 --> 00:02:09.093
with huge global ramifications.

00:02:10.093 --> 00:02:12.385
British journalist Clare
Rewcastle Brown grew up

00:02:12.385 --> 00:02:14.885
in the Malaysian state of Sarawak.

00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:17.801
In 2010, she set up the Sarawak Report

00:02:17.801 --> 00:02:20.593
to expose corruption in
the country of her birth.

00:02:20.593 --> 00:02:21.426
I found that I could

00:02:21.426 --> 00:02:23.593
reach the public in Malaysia

00:02:23.593 --> 00:02:25.635
and get through what had been

00:02:25.635 --> 00:02:28.385
a very oppressive media environment,

00:02:28.385 --> 00:02:32.218
to actually get information
to ordinary people in Malaysia

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.135
about how their country was being run.

00:02:35.426 --> 00:02:37.801
1MDB was presented by Najib Razak,

00:02:37.801 --> 00:02:40.468
the new prime minister, as
a wonderful opportunity.

00:02:40.468 --> 00:02:42.260
He was going to raise huge sums of money

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:45.426
for this so-called sovereign
wealth fund to invest,

00:02:45.426 --> 00:02:47.343
he was also the finance
minister of course,

00:02:47.343 --> 00:02:48.301
as well as the prime minister.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.010
So he would be investing the money

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.010
in all sorts of money-making activities

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:54.135
that would then be beneficial

00:02:54.135 --> 00:02:57.468
to Malaysians in need of development.

00:02:57.468 --> 00:02:59.510
But all that money was disappearing,

00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:00.968
there was no accountability

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.843
and by the time I looked at it,

00:03:02.843 --> 00:03:04.718
we're talking about 2014,

00:03:04.718 --> 00:03:08.468
there had been five years
of massive fundraising

00:03:08.468 --> 00:03:10.843
and then a total black hole

00:03:10.843 --> 00:03:12.885
as far as where that money had gone.

00:03:12.885 --> 00:03:16.926
I think we were talking
about an $11 billion deficit,

00:03:16.926 --> 00:03:19.218
unaccounted deficit by 2014.

00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:22.676
There were certain characters associated

00:03:22.676 --> 00:03:25.968
with the fund who were also
dabbling in my area of interest

00:03:25.968 --> 00:03:28.593
which was the rainforest state of Sarawak.

00:03:28.593 --> 00:03:31.426
Particularly a young
Chinese advisor to the fund

00:03:31.426 --> 00:03:33.760
and to the prime minister, named Jho Low.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:35.760
Jho Low in particular had been gaining

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:38.093
an international reputation for himself

00:03:38.093 --> 00:03:40.676
as a massive spender,
catching the headlines

00:03:40.676 --> 00:03:44.135
in New York, Las Vegas,
and indeed Hollywood.

00:03:44.135 --> 00:03:45.468
He was creating a stir.

00:03:45.468 --> 00:03:48.551
He was the highest spender
in all the top nightclubs

00:03:48.551 --> 00:03:52.135
and yet had no explanation,
really, for his wealth.

00:03:52.135 --> 00:03:54.468
As a lot of you in this room know,

00:03:54.468 --> 00:03:56.718
I like to plan my evenings

00:03:56.718 --> 00:03:59.718
and make sure that I always
go to the best parties.

00:03:59.718 --> 00:04:01.843
So those of us who are
looking at this from Malaysia

00:04:01.843 --> 00:04:05.593
were wondering whether
his advisory role at 1MDB

00:04:05.593 --> 00:04:08.426
where all these billions
were not being accounted for,

00:04:08.426 --> 00:04:10.426
might be connected to this acquisition

00:04:10.426 --> 00:04:12.468
of extraordinary wealth by a 26-year-old

00:04:12.468 --> 00:04:14.010
who'd come from nowhere.

00:04:16.926 --> 00:04:18.885
I first got my teeth into this story

00:04:18.885 --> 00:04:21.010
with the launch of a major,

00:04:21.010 --> 00:04:23.093
$100 million Hollywood movie,

00:04:23.093 --> 00:04:24.218
'Wolf of Wall Street'

00:04:24.218 --> 00:04:25.176
which is all about a bunch of

00:04:25.176 --> 00:04:27.010
crooks who'd stolen money
and were spending it.

00:04:27.010 --> 00:04:29.885
The real question is
this, was all this legal?

00:04:29.885 --> 00:04:30.843
Absolutely not.

00:04:30.843 --> 00:04:33.218
Which is exactly what the funders

00:04:33.218 --> 00:04:35.676
of the movie were doing
of course through 1MDB.

00:04:35.676 --> 00:04:37.676
Because I was able to join some dots

00:04:37.676 --> 00:04:41.343
and I realized that the Malaysia
money funding this film,

00:04:41.343 --> 00:04:43.676
more than likely came from this fund

00:04:43.676 --> 00:04:46.801
because the producer of
the movie was none other

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.551
than the son of the
Malaysian prime minister,

00:04:48.551 --> 00:04:49.760
who was in control of the fund

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.260
that was losing all this money.

00:04:51.260 --> 00:04:53.843
Wow, this is an incredible,
incredible honor.

00:04:53.843 --> 00:04:56.260
Riza Aziz and Jho Low even got a shout-out

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:57.385
at the Golden Globes.

00:04:57.385 --> 00:04:59.593
I want to thank Joey, Riz, and Jho thank you

00:04:59.593 --> 00:05:02.010
for being not only collaborators

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:04.385
but taking a risk on this movie.

00:05:09.885 --> 00:05:13.135
So the 1MDB scandal
could not have happened

00:05:14.051 --> 00:05:16.510
on just a localized basis.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:20.093
It was necessary for the ringleader,

00:05:20.093 --> 00:05:21.968
the alleged, you know,
an accused ringleader,

00:05:21.968 --> 00:05:25.510
this Jho Low to find
accomplices and people

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:29.218
that he could deal with in other
countries around the world.

00:05:29.218 --> 00:05:31.968
As you look back and
unwind the development

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:35.510
of 1MDB and who the early partners were,

00:05:35.510 --> 00:05:37.135
there was clearly a certain amount

00:05:37.135 --> 00:05:39.343
of collusion from interested parties

00:05:39.343 --> 00:05:42.635
in Saudi Arabia and the
United Arab Emirates.

00:05:43.593 --> 00:05:45.093
The PetroSaudi data, which was passed

00:05:45.093 --> 00:05:49.093
to me by a whistleblower,
former director of the company,

00:05:49.093 --> 00:05:53.510
it showed the internal
workings behind the original

00:05:53.510 --> 00:05:56.760
setting up of the first
joint venture of 1MDB

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:00.718
with this Saudi shell company

00:06:00.718 --> 00:06:04.051
that was purporting to be an oil company.

00:06:04.051 --> 00:06:07.676
Right at the start of this extended scandal,

00:06:07.676 --> 00:06:09.968
you see the emails which show a bunch

00:06:09.968 --> 00:06:13.010
of young men agreeing
to pull off this scam.

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:14.551
But at the end of the
letter, they said, of course

00:06:14.551 --> 00:06:16.635
we would also be willing to act as a front

00:06:16.635 --> 00:06:19.260
if that would be useful for
some of your operations?

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.926
So it was all there, along

00:06:20.926 --> 00:06:23.718
with the data that showed
the transfers of money.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.760
The initial deal, the
PetroSaudi bond deal

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:29.885
and joint venture,

00:06:29.885 --> 00:06:32.051
siphoned nearly $2 billion out of the fund.

00:06:32.051 --> 00:06:34.801
That was the first information
I got hard data on.

00:06:38.176 --> 00:06:40.551
Jho Low has been charged
in the United States

00:06:40.551 --> 00:06:44.051
with being basically the
ringleader of this fraud.

00:06:44.051 --> 00:06:45.926
The guy who orchestrated it, even though

00:06:45.926 --> 00:06:48.010
he had no title within 1MDB.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.218
I've been asked whether or not he's like

00:06:49.218 --> 00:06:51.885
a brilliant guy or, you
know, criminal genius?

00:06:51.885 --> 00:06:53.010
I don't think so.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:56.010
It's more, he's financially
very sophisticated.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:58.593
He understood, according
to the charging documents

00:06:58.593 --> 00:07:01.176
in the U.S. how to setup shell companies

00:07:01.176 --> 00:07:03.301
and how to hide the
identity of certain entities

00:07:03.301 --> 00:07:07.718
and to create that first
level of obfuscations.

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:15.010
People like Jho Low and some
other individuals were able to

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:16.968
construct an elaborate set of deceptions

00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:20.176
and shell companies that
sounded just like real companies

00:07:20.176 --> 00:07:24.093
in order to divert the money,
launder it, cover it up,

00:07:24.093 --> 00:07:26.510
and make it appear as
though everything was fine.

00:07:28.135 --> 00:07:30.926
Jho Low was very smart
about covering his tracks.

00:07:30.926 --> 00:07:32.385
One of the first things he did,

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:36.760
right when 1MDB was getting
up and running in 2009,

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:40.468
Jho Low basically established an account

00:07:40.468 --> 00:07:44.135
at a bank or a company in the
Seychelles called Good Star.

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:47.593
After, you know, the
deal was struck to invest

00:07:47.593 --> 00:07:49.301
in this joint venture with sign-off

00:07:49.301 --> 00:07:50.760
from the 1MDB board,

00:07:50.760 --> 00:07:53.968
a mysterious loan obligation appears

00:07:53.968 --> 00:07:58.260
that $700 million of the first $1 billion

00:07:58.260 --> 00:08:00.843
committed to this
venture is going to go to

00:08:00.843 --> 00:08:02.801
pay back a loan from PetroSaudi,

00:08:02.801 --> 00:08:05.426
the U.S. government discovered
that there was no such loan,

00:08:05.426 --> 00:08:08.385
but under the excuse
that a $700 million loan

00:08:08.385 --> 00:08:11.468
had to be paid immediately out
of the first billion dollars,

00:08:11.468 --> 00:08:13.926
a transfer took place from

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:17.551
1MDB's primary bank to, it
was said, it was described,

00:08:17.551 --> 00:08:18.676
it was going to go to PetroSaudi,

00:08:18.676 --> 00:08:20.010
but in fact, it went to this

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.010
small shell company called Good Star.

00:08:22.010 --> 00:08:24.010
And the ownership was hidden,

00:08:24.010 --> 00:08:26.218
it was a like one share, a bearer bond,

00:08:26.218 --> 00:08:27.926
that was owned by Jho Low.

00:08:27.926 --> 00:08:29.510
But none of that was obvious.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:33.010
So he was smart enough to
disguise that first transaction

00:08:33.010 --> 00:08:34.885
and have a cover story
that Good Star was actually

00:08:34.885 --> 00:08:36.426
the name of the venture.

00:08:36.426 --> 00:08:39.093
Perhaps the most famous
example of Jho Low's

00:08:39.093 --> 00:08:41.926
ability to disguise, hide, or obscure

00:08:41.926 --> 00:08:45.426
the source or the destination of the funds

00:08:45.426 --> 00:08:49.093
was an outfit that he, you
know, one of his colleagues came

00:08:49.093 --> 00:08:51.635
up with called Blackstone Asia Real Estate

00:08:51.635 --> 00:08:53.968
which sounds remarkably like a, you know,

00:08:53.968 --> 00:08:58.301
very successful U.S. private
equity firm; Blackstone.

00:08:58.301 --> 00:09:00.510
But it has nothing to do
with the real Blackstone.

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:02.760
It was clearly, it was
just a shell company

00:09:02.760 --> 00:09:05.301
that used the name
Blackstone to sort of give it

00:09:05.301 --> 00:09:07.260
a level of credibility.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:09.426
You know, this happened
over and over again

00:09:09.426 --> 00:09:13.551
coming up with bogus
names that sounded good

00:09:13.551 --> 00:09:16.260
or that sounded like,
or might be similar to

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:20.301
so that the banks who were unknowingly

00:09:20.301 --> 00:09:21.801
basically passing along money

00:09:21.801 --> 00:09:23.510
from one company to another

00:09:23.510 --> 00:09:25.968
it wouldn't raise any obvious red flags.

00:09:25.968 --> 00:09:27.801
Today, the Department of Justice

00:09:27.801 --> 00:09:30.801
has filed a civil complaint
seeking to forfeit

00:09:30.801 --> 00:09:35.218
and recover more than $1
billion in assets associated

00:09:35.218 --> 00:09:38.260
with an international
conspiracy to launder funds

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:42.760
stolen from 1 Malaysia
Development Berhad or 1MDB.

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.760
What makes this such a potent

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:48.635
and devastatingly successful
theft, if you will,

00:09:48.635 --> 00:09:51.051
is basically he had the support of the

00:09:51.051 --> 00:09:54.551
government of Malaysia in the
form of the prime minister.

00:09:54.551 --> 00:09:56.343
If somebody has transgressed the law

00:09:56.343 --> 00:09:58.301
then they have to face the music.

00:09:59.801 --> 00:10:01.760
The money spread around the world,

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.926
and a great deal of it,
was laundered in the U.S.

00:10:04.926 --> 00:10:07.801
You can see this
extraordinary constellation

00:10:07.801 --> 00:10:11.635
of luxury properties and
homes in Beverly Hills,

00:10:11.635 --> 00:10:13.760
in New York and in London.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:17.343
Famous pieces of art, luxury boats,

00:10:17.343 --> 00:10:19.593
gambling sprees in Las Vegas.

00:10:19.593 --> 00:10:22.051
It's one thing for us to
care about money being looted

00:10:22.051 --> 00:10:24.593
from people in countries around the world,

00:10:24.593 --> 00:10:26.968
but also when that
money's coming to the U.S.

00:10:26.968 --> 00:10:28.135
and coursing through our system,

00:10:28.135 --> 00:10:31.343
all this dirty money is
a major cause of concern.

00:10:32.301 --> 00:10:33.301
As pressure mounted on

00:10:33.301 --> 00:10:35.926
the Malaysian prime minister Najib Razak,

00:10:35.926 --> 00:10:38.718
he was ousted from power in May, 2018.

00:10:39.343 --> 00:10:41.968
The new prime minister Mahathir Mohamad,

00:10:41.968 --> 00:10:44.926
wins partly on a platform that
calls for an investigation

00:10:44.926 --> 00:10:47.093
into the missing billions from 1MDB.

00:10:47.093 --> 00:10:48.968
There are many charges

00:10:48.968 --> 00:10:52.010
that can be proven against those involved.

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.343
Soon after the election,

00:10:53.343 --> 00:10:54.885
police raid properties linked to

00:10:54.885 --> 00:10:57.551
Mr. Najib and his wife, Rosmah Mansor,

00:10:57.551 --> 00:11:00.510
and seize hundreds of
boxes of luxury goods.

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.176
We have sealed the bags, but we
know they contain money,

00:11:03.176 --> 00:11:05.135
and we know they contain jewelry.

00:11:05.135 --> 00:11:08.093
Police carted away 284 boxes

00:11:08.093 --> 00:11:10.426
containing luxury handbags and

00:11:10.426 --> 00:11:14.218
72 bags stuffed with cash and jewelry.

00:11:14.218 --> 00:11:16.218
The haul, which authorities later value

00:11:16.218 --> 00:11:18.551
at $273 million,

00:11:18.551 --> 00:11:21.343
includes 567 handbags,

00:11:21.343 --> 00:11:25.968
423 watches, 234 pairs of sunglasses,

00:11:25.968 --> 00:11:27.926
and 14 tiaras.

00:11:28.593 --> 00:11:33.135
In amongst the trinkets
was $29 million in cash.

00:11:33.135 --> 00:11:34.843
The couple maintain the luxury goods

00:11:34.843 --> 00:11:36.093
were gifts,

00:11:36.093 --> 00:11:39.301
and that the cash was political donations.

00:11:39.301 --> 00:11:41.593
The country and the people suffer.

00:11:41.593 --> 00:11:44.635
We must get hold of every cent

00:11:44.635 --> 00:11:47.176
that has been taken out from the country.

00:11:47.885 --> 00:11:50.343
After facing trial for
just some of the charges,

00:11:50.343 --> 00:11:52.051
Najib Razak has been sentenced to

00:11:52.051 --> 00:11:55.760
12 years in prison and fined $50 million.

00:11:56.176 --> 00:11:57.885
He's appealing the decision.

00:11:57.885 --> 00:11:59.760
What do you say to those who say

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:02.010
that you've acted
dishonestly about the funds?

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:03.760
You know, you've been
called all sorts of things,

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:04.760
including a thief.

00:12:04.760 --> 00:12:06.760
What's your response to that?

00:12:06.760 --> 00:12:08.176
There's no evidence of that.

00:12:08.176 --> 00:12:11.051
I mean, you cannot just,
you know, accuse somebody.

00:12:11.051 --> 00:12:12.801
But you have admitted
that the funds did end

00:12:12.801 --> 00:12:14.176
up in your accounts even though it was

00:12:14.176 --> 00:12:16.718
a donation from the Saudi government.

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:19.426
Yeah. It's been,
it's been cleared,

00:12:19.426 --> 00:12:20.926
there's been no wrongdoing.

00:12:20.926 --> 00:12:23.843
There is an appeal process in Malaysia,

00:12:23.843 --> 00:12:27.135
which is extremely lenient
towards the rich and powerful

00:12:27.135 --> 00:12:28.718
and which continues for years.

00:12:28.718 --> 00:12:31.593
And so therefore Najib
continues to walk free

00:12:32.468 --> 00:12:34.843
and he indeed continues to vote

00:12:34.843 --> 00:12:38.135
in Parliament while his case is under appeal.

00:12:38.718 --> 00:12:41.426
The 1MDB case is far from over.

00:12:41.426 --> 00:12:43.968
It's spread to all corners of the globe.

00:12:43.968 --> 00:12:45.968
Jho Low is a fugitive and there's

00:12:45.968 --> 00:12:48.301
plenty of money still missing.

00:12:48.301 --> 00:12:50.468
Not to mention the
amount Malaysia is paying

00:12:50.468 --> 00:12:53.635
in interest on those
original shady bond deals.

00:12:53.635 --> 00:12:57.926
More than $11 billion of
debt racked up in five years.

00:12:57.926 --> 00:12:58.968
There are a lot of people, you know, when

00:12:58.968 --> 00:13:01.843
you talk about it, you know,
their eyes just glaze over.

00:13:01.843 --> 00:13:03.718
It's numbers that we're talking about.

00:13:03.718 --> 00:13:05.468
Hundreds of millions, billions of dollars,

00:13:05.468 --> 00:13:09.051
financial concepts that not
all people are familiar with.

00:13:09.051 --> 00:13:11.468
Ultimately when this
type of thing happens,

00:13:11.468 --> 00:13:14.260
the people who benefit are just
that, that cream at the top

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:17.635
the kleptocrats and the people
who lose, the people who

00:13:17.635 --> 00:13:20.468
remain impoverished are
the people who were like,

00:13:20.468 --> 00:13:21.968
nominally intended to benefit

00:13:21.968 --> 00:13:24.468
from the development of the oil wells

00:13:24.468 --> 00:13:27.135
or the mining concession or whatever.

00:13:28.635 --> 00:13:31.301
The scandal has revealed just
how easily money laundering

00:13:31.301 --> 00:13:35.260
can take place and how
far corruption can reach.

00:13:35.260 --> 00:13:37.843
The complicity of the
global financial system

00:13:37.843 --> 00:13:39.926
continues to be exposed.

00:13:42.385 --> 00:13:45.176
The department filed
criminal charges in New York

00:13:45.176 --> 00:13:47.051
against the Goldman Sachs group

00:13:47.051 --> 00:13:49.010
and its Malaysian subsidiary,

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:51.718
charging each with conspiracy to violate

00:13:51.718 --> 00:13:53.468
the anti-bribery provisions

00:13:53.468 --> 00:13:55.885
of the foreign corrupt practices act.

00:13:55.885 --> 00:13:57.051
Malaysian and Goldman agreed on

00:13:57.051 --> 00:13:59.843
a settlement of $3.9 billion.

00:13:59.843 --> 00:14:01.718
Financial scandal after financial scandal

00:14:01.718 --> 00:14:03.260
involving big banks.

00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:06.343
To be able to divert that much money

00:14:06.343 --> 00:14:09.426
from basically a government
sponsored enterprise

00:14:09.426 --> 00:14:12.051
and then use a network of global banks

00:14:12.051 --> 00:14:13.343
is just astounding.

